WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.534
(playful music)

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:05.294
- [Voiceover] This is
BammBamm. He's a Babirusa.

00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:07.544
Yes, that is a real animal.

00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:10.904
A member of the pig family,

00:00:10.904 --> 00:00:12.607
this prehistoric-looking creature

00:00:12.607 --> 00:00:16.783
is native to the small
Indonesian island of Sulawesi.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.701
In males, the upper canine
teeth grow straight up

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.581
through the flesh of its own snout

00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:25.891
and curve back towards their eyes.

00:00:25.891 --> 00:00:29.473
As they get older, the tusks
can get spectacularly large,

00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:31.879
and on rare occasions have grown so big

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:34.379
as to pierce their own skulls.

00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:39.342
Babirusas spend much of
their time foraging for food,

00:00:39.342 --> 00:00:41.967
eating everything from roots, leaves

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:44.691
and fruits, to meat and grubs.

00:00:44.691 --> 00:00:46.831
His strong jaws are easily capable

00:00:46.831 --> 00:00:49.695
of cracking the hardest of nuts.

00:00:49.695 --> 00:00:51.378
In its native island home, the

00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:53.949
Babirusa has no natural predators.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:56.125
But overhunting and conversion of

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:58.191
their rainforest habitat to farmland

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.187
has reduced their wild population

00:01:00.187 --> 00:01:03.042
to less than a few thousand.

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:05.106
This is the Babirusa.

00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:07.773
(playful music)

